course: dictionary
lesson: 12117
title: Coloration in science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coloration is the pattern and colours on an animal or plant. In a science lesson, the colours often do a job. You can use the context to work out what the word means. «The poison dart frog has bright yellow and blue coloration.» The words bright colours and poison are the clues. Coloration must mean the colours on the frog.
explain: «The stick insect has green coloration that helps it hide among the leaves.» Here the coloration helps the insect survive. It is hard for predators to see it, because it matches the leaves. Always check: swap in the word colours and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Scientists use two useful names. Warning coloration means bright colours on poisonous animals, which tell predators to keep away. Camouflage coloration helps an animal blend in with its surroundings, so it is hidden from predators or prey.
fact: Coloration means the pattern and colours on an animal or plant.
fact: «Warning coloration» means bright colours on poisonous animals.
fact: «Camouflage coloration» helps an animal blend in with its surroundings.
fact: In formal writing, coloration can also mean the general colour of something, or the way something is coloured.
fact: Coloration is usually uncountable, so we talk about the coloration, not many colorations.
exercise: «The poison dart frog has bright coloration.» What does coloration mean here? | The frog's sound when it croaks | The frog's food | *The pattern and colours on the frog | The frog's size
exercise: What is the name for bright colours on a poisonous animal? | *Warning coloration | Stripes | Shelter | Camouflage coloration
exercise: «The stick insect has green coloration that helps it hide among leaves.» Why is this coloration useful? | *It helps the insect blend in and stay safe | It makes the insect louder | It makes the insect easy to spot | It helps the insect fly faster
test: «The owl's brown and grey coloration helps it blend into the tree bark.» What is the main purpose of this coloration? | To keep the owl warm | *Camouflage | To attract a mate | To warn predators to keep away
test: Which word means the pattern and colours of an animal or plant? | Habitat | Diet | Shape | *Coloration
exam: Which word best describes bright colours that warn predators an animal is poisonous? | *Warning | Hunting | Camouflage | Sleeping
